# Late BSA M21 600 cc side-valve outfit with a Watsonian Monaco sports tourer.
#
# The last of the British sidecar outfits: the M21 remained available to special
# order until 1963, and the Monaco was Watsonian's low sports-tourer chair of the
# late 1950s, listed in the 1959 range as a monocoque "sports tourer" with a
# 10 in quick-detachable brake-hub wheel, a low seating position, a wrap-around
# Perspex screen and a rounded tail with the spare wheel.
# https://www.cybermotorcycle.com/gallery/watsonian/Watsonian-1959-Brochure-p12.htm
# https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/BSA_M21
#
# Motorcycle: BSA M21 591 cc side-valve single, 15 bhp, telescopic forks,
# plunger rear suspension, 8 in front brake from 1956.
#
# Dimensions: outfit about 2.10 m long x 1.50 m wide x 1.15 m high, measured
# from the reference photographs; motorcycle wheelbase about 1.38 m; wheels
# 19 in (3.25 front, 3.50 rear, 2.25 chair).
#
# Colours: the M21 was offered in the late 1950s and early 1960s in a small range
# of solid finishes; maroon and black are the two modelled here, matching the
# colours used on the earlier M21 object in this pakset.
#
# Weight: a late variant of the M21, set at 80 in total (maroon 45, black 35) so
# that the M21's overall road presence is split between the two chair types
# rather than doubled. Provisional pending the central rebase.
#
# Speed 80 km/h (50 mph): a game-balance figure for a late 600 cc outfit.
# Comfort 35/200: the Monaco's sprung sidecar wheel and low body give a better
# ride than the Maxstoke outfit's 25-50 range, but it remains an open outfit.
#
# Dates describe when these outfits were seen on British roads: the Monaco from
# 1959-60, the M21 to 1963 and outfits into the later 1960s.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/bsa-m21-monaco-combo.blend in the blends
# repository. References: citycars/references/bsa-m21-monaco/ (gitignored).
# Image credits: 1956 M21 outfit photograph, Thomas's Pics, CC BY 2.0 via
# Wikimedia Commons; Watsonian 1959 brochure scan via Sheldon's EMU, research
# reference only.
# Stage B note: +0.3973 pak units applied after preparation so the motorcycle,
# not the combined bounding box, sits at the tile centre.

obj=citycar
name=BSAM21MonacoCombo(Maroon)
copyright=JamesPetts

DistributionWeight=45
intro_year=1960
intro_month=1
retire_year=1968
retire_month=6
speed=80
class=0,1
maximum_comfortable_journey_minutes=35
maximum_tolerable_journey_minutes=200

